Vid 1

**HOOK**

App launch panniteenga… product ready, aana users zero. Innum 20 WhatsApp groups-la link spam panna poreengala? Stop!

**LOCK-IN ZONE**

Indha 5 places-la unga product-ku match aana audience-a reach pannalaam. 

**POINT 1 — REDDIT**

First, Reddit-la `r/SideProject`.

Just “Try my app” nu link mattum podaadheenga. Enna problem solve panreenga, demo enga irukku, unga app-la enna improve pannanum-nu oru specific question kelunga.

**POINT 2 — HACKER NEWS**

Second, Hacker News-oda **Show HN**.

Idhu working product-ku. Landing page mattum illaama, people actually try panna mudinja better. Technical details-a explain pannunga; comments-ku reply panna ready-a irunga.

**RE-HOOK**

Aana oru myth break pannalaam. Product Hunt-la Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday dhaan best-nu fixed rule illa. Neenga prepare panni launch day-la active-a irukka mudiyura day dhaan important!

**POINT 3 — PRODUCT HUNT**

Third, Product Hunt. Clear demo, product story, first comment—idhula focus pannunga. Upvote kekkaadheenga; genuine feedback kelunga.

**POINT 4 — INDIE HACKERS**

Fourth, Indie Hackers. Product directory-la add pannunga. Unga product yaarukku useful, enna problem solve pannudhu-nu explain pannunga.

**POINT 5 — DEVHUNT / NICHE COMMUNITY**

Fifth, developer tool-na DevHunt try pannunga. Vera app-na, unga target users already discuss panra niche community-a choose pannunga.

**CLOSING**

Important: ellaa places-layum same post copy-paste pannadheenga. Visits mattum illa, sign-ups and actual usage-um track pannunga.

**CTA**

Ovvoru platform-kum enna post pannanum-nu sample templates-oda resource pack ready. Adhukku “Resource” nu comment pannunga!



Vid 2

**HOOK**

Ellarum AI tools kathukittu irukkaanga… aana AI Engineering-la stand out aaganum na, nee vera level-la think pannanum!”

**LOCK-IN ZONE**

Oru research paper-a reproduce pannunga. Oru real open-source project-ku contribute pannunga. Rendum GitHub-la irundha mattum podhaadhu—enna pannenga, eppadi verify panneenga-nu kaamikkanum.

**POINT 1 — REPLICATE A PAPER**

First, oru small AI research paper choose pannunga. Papers With Code link ippo Hugging Face Papers-ku redirect aagudhu. Paper-oda official code, dataset, reported metric ellam check pannunga.

Coding agent-kitta full project one shot-la ezhudha sollaama, smaller tasks-a break panna sollunga. First baseline run pannunga; apram method implement pannunga.

**POINT 2 — CONTRIBUTE TO OPEN SOURCE**

Second, DeepEval illa ZenML maadhiri project-la contribution try pannunga. Current GitHub issues-la `good first issue` label irukka-nu paarunga. Contribution guide padichittu, small documentation fix illa test-related issue start pannalaam.

**RE-HOOK**

Aana important point: code run aayiduchu-nu paper reproduce panniten-nu solla mudiyadhu! Reported result-um unga result-um compare pannirukkeengala?

**POINT 3 — SHOW THE ACTUAL RESULT**

Paper-la expected metric enna? Unga experiment-la enna vandhuchu? Dataset, split, settings same-aa? Difference irundha adhaiyum explain pannunga. Result match aagala-na hide pannaama reason investigate pannunga.

**POINT 4 — MAKE YOUR GITHUB REPRODUCIBLE**

README-la setup steps, dependencies, run command, results table, limitations ellam include pannunga. Open-source PR submit pannumbodhu enna change panneenga, endha tests run panneenga-nu clearly sollunga.

**CLOSING**

Project count-a vida, unga work-a explain panni verify panna mudiyuradhu dhaan stronger evidence.

**CTA**

Paper replication prompt, result-comparison checklist, DeepEval and ZenML links ellam resource pack-la irukku. Adhukku “PROOF” nu comment pannunga!
